RF.put("questb:b16",{"8656":{"id":8656,"t":"Striker's Hauberk","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the the Carapace of the Old God, 2 Idols of Life, 5 Gold Scarabs and 5 Clay Scarabs to Vethsera inside Ahn'Qiraj. You must also attain Honored reputation with the Brood of Nozdormu to complete this quest.\nCarapace of the Old God C'Thun in Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n2 Idol of Life Vekniss Soldier 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Stinger 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Gold Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Clay Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\nReach 9000 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","desc":"The unmentionable Old God slowly awakens from his slumber beneath Ahn'Qiraj. The terrible fate that awaits Azeroth could come in days or years; time has no meaning for beings of his power.\nWhen the stars are favorable, he will lash out against all living beings with terrible wrath. You must find him before then and find a way to bring his existence to an end.\nDo this and bring me a piece of his husk. I shall grant you armor no mortal has ever worn... armor fit for one who has slain a god!","rew":"You will receive:\nStriker's Hauberk\nExperience: 9,950\n+200 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","back":"At his dwelling in Ahn'Qiraj, dread C'Thun awaits in slumber.","done":"I did not expect you to return from your attempt, ‹name›.\nYou've fulfilled a destiny greater than that of most immortal beings.\nBy slaying C'Thun you've not only saved all of Azeroth, you've also tipped the scales of cosmic events beyond your comprehension.\nAccept this breastplate as a symbol of the glory and burden that will come as a consequence of your actions.\nMay its power aid you in the challenges that await you, god-slayer!\nStart Vethsera Ahn'Qiraj Temple End Vethsera Ahn'Qiraj Temple Level 60 , requires level 60 Difficulty 60 Side Both factions Class Hunter Type Raid Shareable Yes Repeatable Yes Quest ID 8656\nThe chain\n2 quests at level 60, 16,550 XP in all.\n1 [ 60 ] Mortal Champions\nKandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n6,600 XP\n2 [ 60 ] Striker's Hauberk this quest\nBring the the Carapace of the Old God, 2 Idols of Life, 5 Gold Scarabs and 5 Clay Scarabs to Vethsera inside Ahn'Qiraj.\nVethsera Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n9,950 XP","cats":["ahnqiraj"]},"656":{"id":656,"t":"Summoning the Princess","lv":50,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Go to the Shards of Myzrael, summon her and defeat her.\nGather her Eldritch Shackles and bind them to the Shards of Myzrael.\nEldritch Shackles Myzrael\nProvided: Scroll of Myzrael","desc":"You must defeat Myzrael before she grows in strength. If you do not, then once she has gathered enough power she will challenge her captors! There are some who think they can control her, but if she can be controlled then why did the giants chain her in the first place??\nCrazy logic, eh?\nTo defeat her, summon her at the Shards of Myzrael where you first spoke with her. Defeat her and gather her Eldritch Shackles, then bind them to the Shards of Myzrael.\nDo that, and she will again be trapped.","rew":"You will receive:\nPulsating Crystalline Shard\nExperience: 7,100","back":"The Shards of Myzrael are now strangely quiet.","done":"As the eldritch shackles are placed around the Shards, an unhuman wail is heard from far below. The scream is followed by a roar.\nThe Shards of Myzrael no longer invoke feelings of warmth and security as they once did. Now they pulse with an open menace... as if the thing beneath them holds ill will toward the surface.\nBadlands Arathi Highlands","pins":[{"z":"Badlands","x":51.4,"y":76.9,"n":"Theldurin the Lost","s":1},{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":62.5,"y":33.7,"n":"Shards of Myzrael","e":1}],"cats":["arathi-highlands"]},"1056":{"id":1056,"t":"Journey to Stonetalon Peak","lv":18,"min":18,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to Keeper Albagorm on Stonetalon Peak.","desc":"The forest spirits tell me you are brave and willing to travel.\nTo the south, not far from Mystral Lake, there lies a tunnel named The Talondeep Path. Through this tunnel you will come to an area known as Windshear Crag in the Stonetalon Mountains. Once there, journey to the southwest past Cragpool Lake and then north, up the steep slope until you reach Stonetalon Peak.\nThere awaits Keeper Albagorm. Heed his bidding, ‹race›.\nThe journey will be perilous.","rew":"Experience: 675\n+50 reputation with Darnassus","done":"Alas, you arrive. I see Faldreas has listened to the forest spirits...\nAshenvale Stonetalon Mountains","pins":[{"z":"Ashenvale","x":35.8,"y":49.1,"n":"Faldreas Goeth'Shael","s":1},{"z":"Stonetalon Mountains","x":37.1,"y":8.1,"n":"Keeper Albagorm","e":1}],"cats":["ashenvale"]},"976":{"id":976,"t":"Supplies to Auberdine","lv":24,"min":19,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Delgren the Purifier at Maestra's Post after seeing Feero safely through Ashenvale Forest.","desc":"Delgren has asked me to deliver messages and supplies to Sentinel Starbreeze in Auberdine, but I am loathe to leave on my own. Dangerous foes operate in the forest, and I do not wish to risk letting these supplies and information fall into the wrong hands.\nIf you and others could act as my guards, I could leave now. With your protection, I have no doubt that we can see these goods safely to Auberdine.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nEverglow Lantern Chestplate of Kor\nMoney: 50 0 gold, 50 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,900\n+200 reputation with Darnassus","back":"The Sentinels have a great need for supplies to reinforce themselves in Darkshore.","done":"You have done well today, ‹class›. The items we sent to aid Auberdine will be of immediate use in dealing with the dark threats that infest the forest.\nTake these with my heartfelt thanks.","pins":[{"z":"Ashenvale","x":26.2,"y":38.9,"n":"Feero Ironhand","s":1},{"z":"Ashenvale","x":26.2,"y":38.7,"n":"Delgren the Purifier","e":1}],"cats":["ashenvale"]},"5536":{"id":5536,"t":"A Land Filled with Hatred","lv":47,"min":45,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill 6 Haldarr Satyr, 2 Haldarr Tricksters, 2 Haldarr Felsworn and then return to Loh'atu on the border of Ashenvale.\nHaldarr Satyr slain : 0/ 6\nHaldarr Trickster slain : 0/ 2\nHaldarr Felsworn slain : 0/ 2","desc":"The satyr, a disfigured, evil aspect of the night elves, now infect the sacred lands once traveled by Cenarius. I cannot speak for the night elves when it comes to all the atrocities those demonic creatures have committed, but I have sworn an oath to the Earthmother to aid the elves in ridding the land of such a nuisance.\nI am sure you would prove yourself if you aided me in purging them.\nNortheast of here, you can find the Haldarr clan. Return to me after you've tested yourself against their power.","rew":"Money: 70 0 gold, 70 silver, 0 copper Experience: 4,200","back":"How goes your battle against the satyr, ‹class›?\nAre they as strong as you thought? Stronger? Or perhaps they were nothing to your own might.","done":"Well done, ‹class›. I see you're not only skilled but cunning. To defeat such creatures is a testament to your loyalty to the tenants of the Earthmother, even if you do not recognize her as your own deity. She is in all things on this planet and beyond. Her eyes, one dark and one light, travel across the skies always gazing down upon us.\nPlease, take this small amount of coin in appreciation for what you have done.","pins":[{"z":"Azshara","x":11.4,"y":78.2,"n":"Loh'atu","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["azshara"]},"97936":{"id":97936,"t":"Camping 101 skinning","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Yonn Deepcut in Bloodhoof Village to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.\nRaise your skinning skill to 20","desc":"Being able to skillfully harvest the skins and hides of fallen beasts is one of the more valuable skills an adventurer can possess.\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Camp Chair for your camp. Sometimes it's important to just take a load off, and you can use some of those hides you've gathered to make a comfy chair to sit in. A bit of relaxation can help ensure that you are at your peak condition and can strike where it counts the next time you find yourself in a dust-up.","done":"There you have it, you can now craft your very own Camp Chair. Most folk don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics.","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":46.2,"y":67.2,"n":"Kaga Wildhoof","s":1},{"z":"Mulgore","x":45.4,"y":57.8,"n":"Yonn Deepcut","e":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"96656":{"id":96656,"t":"The adventurer","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak to Eleanor Shackleton near Brill.","desc":"‹name›, you have proven yourself trustworthy in your endeavors against the Scarlet Crusade so far. That is why I am now entrusting you with an unusual task.\nI've heard of a new adventurer down the road by Brill. Go and see what she's doing.","done":"I'm not affiliated with the Scarlet Crusade, if you couldn't tell. I'm just an adventurer stopping by before my next venture into the wilderness.\nHey, you've got the look of an adventurer yourself. How would you like to learn about camping?","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":32,"y":66,"n":"Executor Arren","s":1},{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":57.2,"y":55.4,"n":"Eleanor Shackleton","e":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"94256":{"id":94256,"t":"Craftsmans writ frost protection potion","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Frost Protection Potion\nFrost Protection Potion","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Frost Protection Potion, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Frost Protection Potion Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94256","cats":["crafting"]},"94336":{"id":94336,"t":"Craftsmans writ lifelike mechanical toad","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Lifelike Mechanical Toad\nLifelike Mechanical Toad","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Lifelike Mechanical Toad, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Lifelike Mechanical Toad Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94336","cats":["crafting"]},"7936":{"id":7936,"t":"50 Tickets - Last Year's Mutton","lv":60,"min":45,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Item #19182","rew":"You will receive:\nLast Year's Mutton","back":"Step right up, step right up! If you have tickets from the Darkmoon Faire you'd like redeemed, then just say so! You can redeem tickets in various denominations for wondrous and fantastic prizes. Don't be shy, give it a try!\nItem #19182 (50)","done":"Here you go, here you go! A prize fit for a king! Congratulations to you, my friend!\nIf you have more tickets you'd like to turn in, then please let me know! For as long as the Darkmoon Faire is here, I'll redeem your tickets.\nMulgore Elwynn Forest","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":38.2,"y":44.7,"n":"Gelvas Grimegate","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":41.5,"y":68.9,"n":"Gelvas Grimegate","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["darkmoon-faire"]},"98896":{"id":98896,"t":"Darkspear islands clash","lv":39,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Level 39\n3 Darkspear Islands Mark of Honor\nAlterac Mountains Arathi Highlands Ashenvale Stormwind City Ironforge Darnassus","pins":[{"z":"Alterac Mountains","x":39.4,"y":82.2,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":45.6,"y":45.8,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Ashenvale","x":61.8,"y":83.8,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":79.4,"y":18,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Ironforge","x":69.8,"y":90,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":58,"y":34.4,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["darkspear-islands"]},"1456":{"id":1456,"t":"The Karnitol Shipwreck","lv":39,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Karnitol's Satchel and return it to Kreldig Ungor in Desolace.\nKarnitol's Satchel Slitherblade Sea Witch 20 % , Slitherblade Tidehunter 20 %","desc":"Intriguing.\nWell, we might not be without hope quite yet.\nAlong that same coast, but to the north near Ranazjar Isle, there're night elf ruins at the bottom of the ocean. A tribe of naga, the Slitherblade, make that their home. I think that'd be our best bet.\nIf a scouting party went that far south, then they must've been pretty powerful. If you're gonna find Karnitol's belongings, I'd start with the more powerful naga: the tidehunters or sea witches.","rew":"Experience: 3,000\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","back":"No offense to whoever Nijel is, but this camp ain't the most comfortable place I've spent a night, if you know what I mean, ‹name›.","done":"This is great, ‹name›! You found Karnitol's belongings!\nThose blasted naga, always causing trouble. I think I'd rather spend my life at war with the Horde than have to go against their kind. You've done a great service to the Reclaimers.","pins":[{"z":"Desolace","x":66.2,"y":9.6,"n":"Kreldig Ungor","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["desolace"]},"816":{"id":816,"t":"Lost But Not Forgotten","lv":11,"min":8,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring a sign of Kron's fate to Misha Tor'kren at the farmstead northwest of Razor Hill.\nKron's Amulet Dreadmaw Crocolisk 10 % , Corrupted Dreadmaw Crocolisk 10 %","desc":"‹name›, please, can you help me? My son Kron went hunting days ago, and he still hasn't returned. He went west towards the Barrens to hunt crocolisks along Southfury River. I fear the worst.\nAs strong as he was, his stubborn pride has always drawn him into trouble. I warned him that the crocolisks were powerful and vicious. He grew angry and stormed off.\nIf you can't find him, at least bring me a sign of his fate... even if you have to open up the stomach of every crocolisk along the Southfury's banks.","rew":"You will receive:\nHandsewn Cloak\nExperience: 875\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar\n+100 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"I pray that Kron will return to me, but I'm almost certain I know his fate already.","done":"Oh, my son... my beautiful son.\nUncertain of my son's fate, I have tormented myself since he left. Now that I know what's happened, perhaps I can finally begin to mourn.\nThank you, ‹name›. Please take this. I was going to give it to Kron as a gift when he returned successful. Now that I know he is dead, I cannot bear to look at it.","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":43.1,"y":30.2,"n":"Misha Tor'kren","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["durotar"]},"9136":{"id":9136,"t":"Savage Flora","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Rayne at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands wants 30 Savage Fronds.\n30 Savage Frond Razorlash 54 % , Bloodpetal Trapper 46.5 % , Bloodpetal Lasher 44.8 % , Bloodpetal Flayer 44.6 % and 4 more","desc":"I make a special type of armor for the brave heroes that enter Naxxramas known as Dreamwalker. They are able to provide me with most of the materials I require but I am always looking for those able to retrieve savage fronds from the flora of our world.\nYou may think of this job as beneath you, but without the fronds, the armor could not be made.\nI am also in a unique position to pay you with an insignia of your choice as both the Dawn and the Crusade supply me with funds.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nInsignia of the Crusade Insignia of the Dawn\nExperience: 6,600\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"I have intimate knowledge of the flora in our world. Do you require direction?","done":"I am much obliged, ‹name›.\n<Rayne bows.>\nPlease remember that I am always acceptINg fronds.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.4,"y":49.3,"n":"Rayne","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"16":{"id":16,"t":"Give Gerard a Drink","lv":1,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Refreshing Spring Water Delmanis the Hated , Dalaran Brewmaster , Water Barrel , Battered Chest 35 % and 4 more","rew":"You will receive:\nShiny Red Apple","back":"Farming is thirsty work, and I'm always looking for refreshing spring water.\nIf you have any, then I'm willing to make a trade.","done":"Thanks, ‹name›! And come back if you want to trade again.","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":43.1,"y":85.5,"n":"Gerard Tiller","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["elwynn-forest"]},"176":{"id":176,"t":"Wanted:  \"Hogger\"","lv":11,"min":5,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Renamed from Wanted: \"Hogger\". New rewards: Apprentice Wizard's Gown.","obj":"Slay the gnoll Hogger and bring his Huge Gnoll Claw to Marshal Dughan.\nHuge Gnoll Claw Hogger","desc":"Wanted: Hogger\nA huge gnoll, Hogger, is prowling the woods in southwestern Elwynn. He has overpowered all attempts at his capture.\nThe Stormwind Army has placed a generous bounty on the Gnoll. To earn the reward, bounty hunters should bring proof of Hogger's demise to Marshal Dughan in Goldshire.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nFootman Tunic Stormwind Guard Leggings Balanced Fighting Stick Apprentice Wizard's Gown\nNew in Forever: Apprentice Wizard's Gown.\nExperience: 875\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Yes, Hogger has been a real pain for me and my men. You have something to report about the beast?","done":"Hah! Well done! I was starting to think no one would take down that monster!\nHere you are, ‹name›. And thanks - that Gnoll was giving me a headache the size of Blackrock Spire!","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":24.5,"y":74.7,"n":"Wanted Poster","s":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":24.6,"y":78.2,"n":"Wanted Poster","s":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":42.1,"y":65.9,"n":"Marshal Dughan","e":1}],"cats":["elwynn-forest"]},"2976":{"id":2976,"t":"A Grim Discovery","lv":45,"min":38,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Crate of Grimtotem Horns to Belgrom Rockmaul in Orgrimmar.\nCrate of Grimtotem Horns\nProvided: Crate of Grimtotem Horns","desc":"What?!\nAh, so I did mention a bounty, didn't I? Well, that'll teach me to open my mouth, won't it?\nYou did the work, so I suppose it is only right you reap the greatest reward from it. Take the horns, I'll have them put in a crate for you. Find Belgrom Rockmaul in the Valley of Honor, he'll want to know what you saw and he'll reward you for your hard work.\nBe well, ‹class›, and thank you again for everything you've done.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nBattlehard Cape Jademoon Orb\nMoney: 65 0 gold, 65 silver, 0 copper Experience: 4,850\n+150 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"Be quick, ‹class›, I have much to complete today.","done":"The Grimtotem!? This is interesting. You say you came across them while hunting in Feralas? Truly?\nMy peers will want to hear your news, ‹class›. Tell me more and I'll count out your coin while you do so.\nAnd before you go, know that I give you thanks for the information you've passed on to me this day.\nFeralas Orgrimmar","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":75.9,"y":42.7,"n":"Krueg Skullsplitter","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":75.2,"y":34.2,"n":"Belgrom Rockmaul","e":1}],"cats":["feralas"]},"496":{"id":496,"t":"Elixir of Suffering","lv":22,"min":19,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Apothecary Lydon of Tarren Mill wants 10 Gray Bear Tongues and some Creeper Ichor.\n10 Gray Bear Tongue Big Samras , Gray Bear 80 % , Vicious Gray Bear 80 % , Elder Gray Bear 80 %\nCreeper Ichor Elder Moss Creeper , Giant Moss Creeper , Forest Moss Creeper , Creepthess","desc":"Ah, another wretched day in Tarren Mill. All of this clean air puts me in such a foul mood, ‹name›.\nThe sooner we can plague the humans here, the better. I've been conducting intense studies on possible killing agents to use in my concoctions but I haven't the time to collect them all.\nIf you want to make yourself of use, procure the following items for me: 10 Gray Bear Tongues and the very rare and hard to find, Creeper Ichor. You'll find both bears and creepers just outside of Tarren Mill.","rew":"Money: 1 50 0 gold, 1 silver, 50 copper Experience: 180\n+25 reputation with Undercity","back":"I see you are back. I hope you were able to gather the agents I need. Another deathless day will put me in such a gloomy mood.","done":"These specimens are perfect. Well, ‹name›, you have managed to bring me the slightest hint of joy on yet another miserable day. Your efforts are appreciated.","pins":[{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":61.4,"y":19.1,"n":"Apothecary Lydon","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["hillsbrad-foothills"]},"416":{"id":416,"t":"Rat Catching","lv":11,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 12 Tunnel Rat Ears to Mountaineer Kadrell in Thelsamar.\n12 Tunnel Rat Ear Tunnel Rat Kobold 50 % , Tunnel Rat Surveyor 50 % , Tunnel Rat Forager 50 % , Tunnel Rat Digger 50 % and 3 more","desc":"We have a real infestation problem to the west. Tunnel rat kobolds have moved into the foothills, setting up dens and fouling our land with their filth!\nWe want them eliminated. Hunt them, bring me their ears and earn their bounty.\nYou can find tunnel rat kobolds and their dens west of Thelsamar, littered along the mountainside.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nBurnt Hide Bracers Cavalier's Boots\nMoney: 4 0 gold, 4 silver, 0 copper Experience: 875\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","back":"Hail, ‹name›. How goes the rat catching?","done":"Ugh! When I asked for those ears I didn't realize they'd smell so bad!\nHere's your reward, ‹name›. Well done.","pins":[{"z":"Loch Modan","x":34.2,"y":47.8,"n":"Mountaineer Kadrell","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["loch-modan"]},"256":{"id":256,"t":"WANTED: Chok'sul","lv":22,"min":17,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. New rewards: Loch Walkers.","obj":"Kill Chok'sul and bring his head to Magistrate Bluntnose of Thelsamar.\nChok'sul's Head Chok'sul","desc":"By order of the Magistrate of Thelsamar:\nChok'sul, the ogre presumed to be the leader and coordinator of attacks against the town of Thelsamar, Stonewrought Dam, and the excavation site, is wanted dead through any means necessary.\nMonetary compensation will be provided when proof is brought to the Magistrate of Chok'sul's death.\nChok'sul was last seen at the ogre encampment in the northeastern part of Loch Modan.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nDurable Chain Shoulders Kimbra Boots Loch Walkers\nNew in Forever: Loch Walkers.\nYou will also receive:\nMinor Channeling Ring\nExperience: 1,750\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","back":"Yes? Is there something I can do for you?","done":"Yech! What is that thing? And why would you bring it...\nBloody--! Is it? Well, Light burn me, is that the head of that bloody ogre? This certainly is a catch then! Here, your reward and the thanks of myself and the people of Thelsamar.","pins":[{"z":"Loch Modan","x":37.3,"y":46.5,"n":"WANTED","s":1},{"z":"Loch Modan","x":34.6,"y":44.5,"n":"Magistrate Bluntnose","e":1}],"cats":["loch-modan"]},"98576":{"id":98576,"t":"Glyphic parchment","lv":1,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Read the Glyphic Parchment and speak with Mai'ah near the entrance to the Den in the Valley of Trials.\nProvided: Glyphic Parchment","desc":"Ah, while you were gone a parchment came for you, ‹name›.\nRead it when you have time. If I'm not mistaken, it came from the mage trainer Mai'ah. She would have words with you when you're ready.","back":"Ya come to Mai'ah ready to learn. Dat be good. Ya got da power to touch da strands of da cosmos, but ya also got da wisdom to know dat you need guidance. I can teach ya da first steps to wield dat power.","done":"Da magic dat flows through you be da greatest power in da universe, but ya must be patient. Wait for da perfect moment to strike. Choose da right response to da problem at hand. If you be smart, and you watch carefully, dere be nothing you can't do.\nWhen ya tink you be ready for trainin', come back to Mai'ah. She teach you what you ready to learn, no problem.","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":42,"y":68.4,"n":"Gornek","s":1},{"z":"Durotar","x":42.4,"y":69,"n":"Mai'ah","e":1}],"cats":["mage"]},"8736":{"id":8736,"t":"The Nightmare Manifests","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Defend Nighthaven from Eranikus. Do not let Keeper Remulos perish. Do not slay Eranikus. Defend yourself. Await Tyrande.","desc":"We must use restraint against Eranikus. We are to redeem him not destroy him.\nTyrande is already en route to assist us in this task. We must weather the dragon's blows and save Nighthaven from certain destruction.\nBe on guard! You and your allies are our only hope.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nDrake Tooth Necklace Drudge Boots\nExperience: 9,950\n+200 reputation with Cenarion Circle\n+200 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","done":"He is redeemed, ‹name›. He now returns to the Dream to right what he alone has done wrong. Eranikus will be a powerful ally to Malfurion and my father.\nThese armaments are for you, ‹name›; given to me by Ysera herself. You would do well to make use of them in your battles against the Qiraji.","pins":[{"z":"Moonglade","x":36.2,"y":41.8,"n":"Keeper Remulos","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["moonglade"]},"3376":{"id":3376,"t":"Break Sharptusk!","lv":5,"min":3,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the head of Chief Sharptusk Thornmantle to Brave Windfeather in Red Cloud Mesa.\nChief Sharptusk Thornmantle's Head Chief Sharptusk Thornmantle","desc":"‹name› - I have heard of you, newcomer. Perhaps it is you that will help us, where others have failed.\nWe tauren have carved a home out of this land, but not without a cost. The Bristleback quilboars of Brambleblade Ravine, led by Chief Sharptusk Thornmantle, have made our lives difficult with their continued war against us. I charge you to bring me the chief's head!\nHe will be found in the ravine to the east in their makeshift village.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nPainted Chain Leggings Nomadic Gloves\nExperience: 675\n+200 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"Sharptusk will trouble us no more once you have brought me proof of his death. It is his head that I seek, ‹name›.\nWe tauren live for the hunt, and there is no greater hunt than against one that is cunning enough to perhaps hunt us back. If you are successful in this task, young one, you will start to learn what I mean.","done":"Justice has been served on this day by your swift actions, ‹name›. Let this deed serve as a warning to all who would threaten our home.\nYou have earned this reward to help you on your sojourn, young ‹class›.","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":44.2,"y":77,"n":"Brave Windfeather","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["mulgore"]},"9056":{"id":9056,"t":"Cryptstalker Headpiece","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Huntsman Leopold at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands will make a Cryptstalker Headpiece if you bring him the following: 1 Desecrated Headpiece, 15 Wartorn Chain Scraps, 4 Arcanite Bars and 2 Nexus Crystals.\nDesecrated Headpiece\n15 Wartorn Chain Scrap Stoneskin Gargoyle 14.4 % in Naxxramas , Infectious Ghoul 13.5 % in Naxxramas , Spirit of Naxxramas 13.3 % in Naxxramas , Living Monstrosity 12.5 % in Naxxramas and 4 more\n4 Arcanite Bar\n2 Nexus Crystal","desc":"I have discovered a use for the carapace of the crypt fiend. I am able to fashion an extremely light and very deadly set of armor by combining the fragments with some of the desecrated magical armors lost in Naxxramas.\nBring me the items I require and I shall fashion for you a suit of armor the likes of which has never before been seen in our world!","rew":"You will receive:\nCryptstalker Headpiece\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"You got some missing parts for the quest please go and get them all!","done":"Exellent ‹name› !\n, you got everything just as i asked and now i can make a Cryptstalker Headpiece.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.7,"y":48.9,"n":"Huntsman Leopold","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"8416":{"id":8416,"t":"Inert Scourgestones","lv":52,"min":50,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Inert Scourgestone to Commander Ashlan Valorfist in Chillwind Point.\nInert Scourgestone\nProvided: Inert Scourgestone","desc":"The evil has been purged from the stones, ‹name›.\nI am aware of Commander Ashlam's plans, and he will require only a single inert stone. Bring it to him so we may bathe the Scourge in righteous fire.","rew":"Experience: 2,550\n+50 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"Was Thal'danis able to cleanse the scourgestones?","done":"You have done as I asked without question, ‹name›.\nTrust is achieved, it seems. Perhaps I can reveal our plan in more detail to you now.","pins":[{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":52.1,"y":83.3,"n":"High Priest Thel'danis","s":1},{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":42.7,"y":84,"n":"Commander Ashlam Valorfist","e":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"8256":{"id":8256,"t":"The Ichor of Undeath","lv":52,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Acquire an Ichor of Undeath for Ogtinc in Azshara. Ogtinc resides atop the cliffs northeast the Ruins of Eldarath.\nIchor of Undeath Deathstalker Agent 17 % , Nathanos Blightcaller 12.5 % , Blood Wraith 10.5 % , Screaming Haunt 10.1 % and 4 more","desc":"For this restorative salve, you must use a simple formula: one part poison, two parts cure. You have acquired one cure, now you must gather the poison.\nPowerful undead, such as the lingering highborne who wander the Ruins of Eldarath, are sometimes so infused with evil that it coalesces into a sickly greenish goo. To the living, this substance is known as ichor of undeath.\nDue to the potency of this vile element, I require only a single ichor.","rew":"Experience: 5,100","back":"We must obtain the ichor quickly. Have you found it?","done":"I cannot say I'm pleased to receive such a wretched substance, but it is a necessary evil. Thank you, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"Azshara","x":42.4,"y":42.6,"n":"Ogtinc","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["priest"]},"8816":{"id":8816,"t":"One Commendation Signet","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Horde Commendation Signet","back":"For those adventurers who have but a single commendation signet, I'll exchange it for a small amount of recognition with Undercity.\nPlease bear in mind that it is better to hand over a stack of ten signets at once; your efforts will receive greater recognition in doing so. We offer a single signet exchange as a service for those who don't have enough for a full stack of ten.\nWith that being said, I stand ready to assist you if you still wish to hand in a single signet.","done":"Very well - your deeds have been entered into the records, and you are duly recognized for your efforts. Keep up the good work, ‹class›.\nIf you have any more signets to hand in, then I am able to assist you further in that regard.\nOrgrimmar Undercity","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":30,"y":70.1,"n":"Darkspear Commendation Officer","s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":61.9,"y":45.3,"n":"Officer Gothena","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["reputation"]},"95216":{"id":95216,"t":"The New Plague","lv":22,"min":16,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its experience counts the level 30 build, which halved what dungeon quests give beyond a normal quest.","obj":"Collect the Highly Toxic Strain from Witherfang in Ruins of Lordaeron for Theodore Griffs in Undercity.\nHighly Toxic Strain","desc":"Welcome to the most vital organ of the Undercity: The Apothecarium! Here we experiment on the most virulent of Azeroth's exotic specimens.\nYou've caught me in a good mood, so I will let you in on my latest investigation. It appears there is a particularly venomous arthropod stalking the ruins above our fair city. Its toxins are said to eat through even undead flesh. How exhilarating!\nI wish to validate these claims. Should you find yourself withering away from its bite, I should love a sample.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nPlaguefang Blight Gloves\nExperience: 5,450","back":"Any fool can tell you the most potent transmission method will always be through the blood.\nI must see this strain for myself!","done":"You killed it??\nHmmph. Lucky for you this should be enough ichor to reverse engineer its properties. You do not wish to be an enemy of the Royal Apothecary Society.\nGet out of my sight!","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":46.6,"y":72,"n":"Theodore Griffs","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ruins-of-lordaeron-dungeon"]},"1536":{"id":1536,"t":"Call of Water","lv":22,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Fill the Empty Red Waterskin at the well in Tarren Mill and return to Brine in the Barrens.\nFilled Red Waterskin\nProvided: Empty Red Waterskin","desc":"Long ago I followed some companions into the Hillsbrad Foothills. We defended ourselves from some tenacious humans who make their home there and we found ourselves in a small town the Forsaken had taken over: Tarren Mill.\nIt was there I found a most peculiar thing: in the center of town was a small well of fresh spring water. I'm not sure the plagued citizens of the town even realize its value--it's a small holy vestige in an unhallowed sea.\nBring me a sample of that water in this waterskin.","rew":"Experience: 1,300","back":"The well remaining pure within the town reminds me of stories told to me when I was younger, ‹name›. Even in times of great pain and sorrow one can find a sliver of hope, a small symbol to rally around. The orc people see Thrall this way. He survived against great odds and rose up to lead our people through his strength and example.\nI'm not sure any orc has suffered as much as he has, but at the same time, I'm not sure any orc is as strong as he is either.","done":"This is good, ‹name›. You're dedicated to the task at hand and have the ability to seek out that which is needed.\nOne more sample is all I need to create the reagent needed for your sapta. Islen will be pleased as well.\nThe Barrens Hillsbrad Foothills","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":43.4,"y":77.4,"n":"Brine","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["shaman"]},"96":{"id":96,"t":"Call of Water","lv":23,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Shard of Water to Islen Waterseer in the Barrens.\nShard of Water\nProvided: Shard of Water","desc":"Take shard. Take shard and give life.\nGive life and understand. Understand water is life... corruption stops life.\nYou protect and give life with water's power.","rew":"You will receive:\nWater Totem\nYou will learn: Healing Stream Totem\nExperience: 2,750","back":"You've returned. Splendid!\nHow went your journey to Silverpine? Did it take you long?\nIt is hard for me to tell if you were successful there because so much of the land has become corrupt. Its stench overwhelms any good that you might have done. But small successes are sometimes as important as large ones. Purifying the water there was instrumental for you, and for all shamans.","done":"This is the proof I asked for. You've done well, ‹name›.\nI am pleased to be the first to congratulate you and give you this... your water totem.\nUse it well, and good luck.\nYour next test will not be for some time, so learn your lessons well. Pure water will not only give life back to those who are injured, but can have many other effects. I suggest you seek out a shaman trainer when you have the time. They might have other spells for you to learn.","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":65.8,"y":43.8,"n":"Islen Waterseer","e":1}],"cats":["shaman"]},"96016":{"id":96016,"t":"The tempests weapons","lv":40,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Deliver the Eye of the Tempest to Bath'rah the Windwatcher in Alterac Mountains.\nProvided: Eye of the Tempest","desc":"Ye did good, and I can see yer itchin' fer yer reward. Sorry tae say, I'm not exactly a dwarf of many possessions.\n<Veyric gestures broadly at his remote location.>\nTell ye what, though. I hear a troll named the Windwatcher lives out in the Alterac Mountains. He's a powerful shaman himself, and an expert in storm elementals. If ye bring that there elemental core to him, I bet he can make ye a weapon worthy of yer victory.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nLightning's Grasp Tidebringer's Claw Rage of the Storm\nYou will also receive:\nElementalist's Guard\nMoney: 50 0 gold, 50 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,150\nLevel 40 , requires level 30 Difficulty 30 36 38 43 51 Side Alliance Class Shaman Quest ID 96016\nThe chain\n5 quests from level 30 to 40, 17,150 XP in all.\n1 [ 30 ] Call of Air\nFind Veyric Thundervein in Arathi Highlands.\nEldrun Stormbreaker Ironforge\n2,450 XP\n2 [ 33 ] Elemental Aid\nDefeat Charlga Razorflank in Razorfen Kraul and collect information on the quilboar's plans.\nVeyric Thunderhame Arathi Highlands\n5,550 XP\n3 [ 38 ] Storm, Earth, and Fire\nCollect 5 Twisted Fire Totems, 5 Twisted Earth Totems, 5 Twisted Air Totems, and 5 Twisted Water Totems for Veyric Thunderhame in Arathi Highlands.\nVeyric Thunderhame Arathi Highlands\n2,850 XP\n4 [ 40 ] Heed My Call\nUse the Twisted Totems to put an end to the quilboar ritual.\nVeyric Thunderhame Arathi Highlands\n3,150 XP\n5 [ 40 ] The Tempest's Weapons this quest\nDeliver the Eye of the Tempest to Bath'rah the Windwatcher in Alterac Mountains.\n3,150 XP","cats":["shaman"]},"8496":{"id":8496,"t":"Bandages for the Field","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 30 Heavy Runecloth Bandages, 30 Heavy Silk Bandages and 30 Heavy Mageweave Bandages to Windcaller Proudhorn at Cenarion Hold in Silithus. You must also bring Logistics Task Briefing X in order to complete this quest.\n30 Heavy Runecloth Bandage sold by Jimmy McWeaksauce\n30 Heavy Mageweave Bandage\n30 Heavy Silk Bandage\nLogistics Task Briefing X\nProvided: Logistics Task Briefing X","desc":"Our supply of bandages in the battlefield is running dangerously low after the recent casualties we have incurred. Obtain a batch of first-aid supplies and deliver them to Windcaller Proudhorn in Cenarion Hold.","rew":"You will receive:\nCenarion Logistics Badge Followup Logistics Assignment\nExperience: 650\n+50 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"You have something for me, ‹name›?","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":51.2,"y":38.3,"n":"Windcaller Proudhorn","e":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"79536":{"id":79536,"t":"Greater friend of the library","lv":35,"min":20,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nField Researcher's Loop Philanthropist's Ring\nMoney: 3 50 0 gold, 3 silver, 50 copper Experience: 280","done":"Thanks to your donations, the library is thriving.\nPlease, take this.\nStormwind City Undercity","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":37.8,"y":80.2,"n":"Garion Wendell","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":73.6,"y":33,"n":"Owen Thadd","e":1}],"cats":["special"]},"86576":{"id":86576,"t":"Bloodfury trinkets","lv":26,"min":18,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring 15 Glittering Sunstones to Mor'rogal.\n15 Glittering Sunstone","desc":"In addition to spreading their filth across the Charred Vale, the Bloodfury harpies gather anything shiny that they can find. I'm told that they collect a variety of golden-yellow sunstones for decoration. I have no use for such trinkets, but Mor'rogal has mentioned using them before.\nWhile you're fighting the harpies of the Vale, keep your eye out for Glittering Sunstones. Bring any that you find to Mor'rogal, up on the hills above us.","rew":"You will receive:\nHarpy Claw Ring\nMoney: 20 0 gold, 20 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,100","pins":[{"z":"Stonetalon Mountains","x":47.2,"y":61,"n":"Maggran Earthbinder","s":1}],"cats":["stonetalon-mountains"]},"336":{"id":336,"t":"A Noble Brew","lv":30,"min":25,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the Black Claw Stout to Lord Wishock in the Hall of Petitioners.\nBlack Claw Stout\nProvided: Black Claw Stout","desc":"Lord Wishock, like all men, has his weaknesses. His happens to be a fondness for liquor. The hypocrisy is astounding. The trite fool spends his days trying to shut down our little \"tavern\" while his nights are spent upstairs, running up a bill he never pays. Well, let's see how Wishock likes this special brew I have prepared for him: Black Claw stout. It's got quite a kick, ‹name›.\nTake it to him and see how he likes it. Most likely the old fool is milling about the Hall of Petitioners.","rew":"Money: 25 0 gold, 25 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,450","back":"Can you not see that I am busy? My words must be heard! I am very important to the future of this Kingdom!\nOh... what have you there? Why it looks like a refreshing drink...","done":"Ah, thank you for bringing me this fine looking stout, servant. Here's a copper for you. Now, out of sight with you and let me enjoy my drink!","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":40.1,"y":85.3,"n":"Zardeth of the Black Claw","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":77.9,"y":48.9,"n":"Lord Baurles K. Wishock","e":1}],"cats":["stormwind-city"]},"576":{"id":576,"t":"Keep An Eye Out","lv":42,"min":37,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Dizzy One-Eye in Booty Bay wants you to retrieve his eye from the Bloodsail Buccaneers.\nDizzy's Eye Bloodsail Swabby 10 % , Bloodsail Deckhand 10 % , Brutus 10 % , Captain Stillwater 10 % and 4 more","desc":"Avast! Who goes there?\nArgh, I am but useless without me special enchanted eye. Bad enough to have lost me eyes in battle in the first place! But by some stroke o' luck we docked in Menethil and a traveling wizard enchanted a special glass eye that let me see again.\nLast night I ended up gettin' jumped by some Bloodsail Buccaneers on me way out. Took me eye, they did! Seems those blokes have found their way to Booty Bay.\nHelp an old sea dog out by gettin' me eye back?","rew":"You will receive:\nDarktide Cape\nExperience: 2,550\n+150 reputation with Booty Bay\n-750 reputation with Bloodsail Buccaneers","back":"Ahoy, me bucko! Might not be able to see but I can smell ye from halfway across port.\nCould really use me eye back. Captain's going to keelhaul me when he finds out me peeper is in the hands of them dirty Bloodsail Buccaneers.\nWhat good is a lookout who can't see? The crow's nest used to be me home...without me deadlights I'd be lucky to scrub the bilge.","done":"Shiver me timbers and timber me shivers! Ye found me beautiful eye! Let's see if she still fits.\nShavas ho! Blimey, I can see!!","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":28.6,"y":75.9,"n":"Dizzy One-Eye","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"4496":{"id":4496,"t":"Bungle in the Jungle","lv":53,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring a Gorishi Scent Gland and 5 Un'Goro Soil samples to Alchemist Pestlezugg in Gadgetzan.\nGorishi Scent Gland Gorishi Wasp 8 % , Gorishi Worker 8 % , Gorishi Reaver 8 % , Gorishi Stinger 8 % and 2 more\n5 Un'Goro Soil Un'Goro Dirt Pile , Gorishi Hive Guard 58.8 % , Gorishi Worker 55.8 % , Gorishi Stinger 55.2 % and 4 more","desc":"My research revealed to me that the silithid are like bees; destroy the queen of the hive, and the rest of should be thrown into disarray. I'll brew a lure that we'll use to bring out the queen; once summoned, you'll take her down.\nFirst though, we need some reagents; we don't want you bungling into the jungle unprepared. Go west to find the silithid hive in Un'Goro Crater and obtain a scent gland from one of the bugs. I'll also need some samples of the native Un'Goro soil.","rew":"Experience: 5,250\n+100 reputation with Gadgetzan","back":"Finding a suitable scent gland might take a bit - the gland can't be damaged, but the process of getting one certainly doesn't lend itself to it. As for the soil, I'd assume it should be easy enough to find.\nAnyway, do you have the items I need to make the lure?","done":"The scent gland, ah yes. The membrane appears intact - excellent. The soil, yes, this should work out perfectly. With my special additions, I should be able to grind all this up into the perfect lure.\nGive me a moment to make the lure, ‹name›. Once it's ready, we'll be able to enact the next step that may hopefully stop the silithid before they overrun Gadgetzan... and the rest of Kalimdor.\nTanaris Un'Goro Crater","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":50.9,"y":27,"n":"Alchemist Pestlezugg","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"8576":{"id":8576,"t":"Translating the Ledger","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"Experience: 650\n+10 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","done":"First things first, ‹name›! We need to figure out what Azuregos wrote in this ledger.\nYou say that he's told you to make an arcanite buoy and that this is the schematic? Strange that he would write this in Draconic. That old goat knows I can't read this nonsense.\nIf this is going to work, I'm going to need my scrying goggles, a five hundred pound chicken and volume II of \"Draconic for Dummies.\" Not necessarily in that order.","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":65.2,"y":18.6,"n":"Narain Soothfancy","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"896":{"id":896,"t":"Miner's Fortune","lv":18,"min":13,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Retrieve the Cats Eye Emerald from one of the Venture Co. Overseers or Enforcers for Wharfmaster Dizzywig at Ratchet.\nCats Eye Emerald Boss Copperplug 10 % , Venture Co. Overseer 10 % , Venture Co. Enforcer 10 %","desc":"Being Wharfmaster of a busy port like Ratchet, I keep my finger on the pulse of information. I know all about the exchange of goods and money between here and Booty Bay.\nThe latest bit of news I've heard is about the Venture Company's Boulder Lode mine northeast of the Sludge Fen. One of the miners discovered an emerald the size of your fist. I know a few buyers who'd be interested in getting their hands on something like that, and I'd be willing to go half and half on its sale.","rew":"You will receive:\nA Sack of Coins\nExperience: 1,700\n+150 reputation with Ratchet","back":"If only we knew which one of the miners had found the emerald, it'd be a walk in the park...","done":"Look at the size of that thing, ‹name›! We're going to be rich! Let's see, according to the rates I've seen on gems going into Undermine, I should be able to figure out your cut--fifty percent, don't worry!\nNow let's see... I think this should do about right. Pleasure doing business with you, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":63.4,"y":38.5,"n":"Wharfmaster Dizzywig","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"1136":{"id":1136,"t":"Frostmaw","lv":37,"min":26,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Frostmaw's Mane to Melor Stonehoof in Thunder Bluff.\nFrostmaw's Mane Frostmaw\nProvided: Kodo Skin Scroll","desc":"‹name›, it is now time for you to travel to far-off lands. You are ready.\nYou now hunt Frostmaw, a yeti in the Alterac Mountains. He is elusive, his white coat blending into the snows of his mountain home. He rarely shows himself.\nBut I will show you how to entice a creature such as he. Here, take this scroll. On it I have written how Frostmaw may be lured.\nNow go, ‹name›. Your journey is long and many challenges lay waiting. When you return with Frostmaw's mane, only then is your task complete.","rew":"You will receive:\nSpirit Hunter Headdress\nExperience: 4,250\n+200 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"Have you been to the Alterac Mountains, ‹name›? Did you face the elusive Frostmaw?","done":"Both strength and cunning were needed to find and defeat Frostmaw, ‹name›. You have both.\nYour path has taken you to the valleys of Thousand Needles and to the high mountains of Alterac. It will one day lead you through all the Earthmother's lands, for such is the way of the hunter.\nThunder Bluff Alterac Mountains","pins":[{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":61.5,"y":80.9,"n":"Melor Stonehoof","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["thunder-bluff"]},"96896":{"id":96896,"t":"A righteous cause","lv":13,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Observe the conversation between Danitha Morr and Leonid Barthalomew the Revered.","desc":"Danitha and I fought against the scourge in the defense of the Undercity when Naxxramas attacked. We lost many good friends that day, including the hero after which this keep was named--Garek Bandarion.\nHe might just have been the first Forsaken to rediscover how to wield the light as a paladin. I am encouraged to see his legacy and potential live on here with Danitha and her cohort.\nIf only the rest of the forsaken felt the same way...","done":"I plan to stay here for a time and speak with more of my friends, but I will return to Light's Hope Chapel in Eastern Plaguelands soon enough. Should you ever find yourself out that way, please do say hello. We could use always use more help from able-bodied adventurers.","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":22,"y":44.8,"n":"Leonid Barthalomew the Revered","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tirisfal-glades"]},"736":{"id":736,"t":"The Star, the Hand and the Heart","lv":44,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the items on Bel'dugur's Note to Keeper Bel'dugur in the Undercity.\nStar of Xil'yeh Grel'borg the Miser\nHand of Dagun Dagun the Ravenous\nThe Legacy Heart Mogh the Undying\nProvided: Bel'dugur's Note","desc":"You need Yagyin's Digest? Your plan, then, is to gather another flock? Of course it is...and of course I will help you, brother/sister.\nBut you must help me too.\nI require three items of power. Bring me these and the digest will be yours.\nI cannot utter the names of these items, but I will write them down.\nGet me the items on this list. If you can do that, then you are truly worthy of opening your own chapter of our order.","rew":"Experience: 5,600","back":"How goes your mission, ‹class›.","done":"I am impressed! You possess great skill, or great fortune, to have gained these relics. Either way, you are an asset to us.\nUndercity Alterac Mountains Stranglethorn Vale Dustwallow Marsh","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":53.7,"y":54.5,"n":"Keeper Bel'dugur","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["undercity"]},"4736":{"id":4736,"t":"In Search of Menara Voidrender","lv":31,"min":31,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Menara Voidrender in the Barrens.","desc":"Ah, hello, ‹name›. You're progressing well in your training. So well in fact that I think you should be rewarded for your hard work--and for not becoming corrupted by the arcane yet.\nIf you're interested, seek out Menara Voidrender in Ratchet. She is currently staying at Strahad Farsan's tower overlooking the town.\nShe's not very friendly, ‹name›, so don't expect any praise. But if you work hard, she'll make sure you're taken care of.","rew":"Experience: 625","done":"Ah, Briarthorn sent you. Good. Then word does reach far enough to find future students. This pleases me.\nIt is typical of our kind, ‹name›, to band together, regardless of race. It is especially important since those we deal with most do not discriminate in their malice if we fail to appease them or control them properly.\nI feel you've learned a great many things, and if you are willing, I would help you create tools to compliment your skills.\nDun Morogh The Barrens","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":59.2,"y":22,"n":"Briarthorn","s":1},{"z":"The Barrens","x":62.5,"y":35.4,"n":"Menara Voidrender","e":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"4976":{"id":4976,"t":"Returning the Cleansed Orb","lv":40,"min":35,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return the Cleansed Infernal Orb to Menara Voidrender in the Barrens.\nCleansed Infernal Orb\nProvided: Cleansed Infernal Orb","desc":"Take the cleansed orb back to Menara in Ratchet, ‹name›. Give her my regards and be safe. I truly hope you are able to withstand the temptation and corruption that is sure to come as you follow your path.\nGood luck.","rew":"Experience: 1,550","back":"How goes your search for Tabetha and the orb, ‹name›?\nTabetha has been more than useful when it comes to matters of the arcane. I'm sure she would have no problem aiding you if you're able to find her.","done":"Well done, ‹name›. This will do nicely.\nThe only thing left for you to do is to decide on which demon you want me to imprison within the cleansed orb. Do that, and you will have a magnificent new item to wield.\nDustwallow Marsh The Barrens","pins":[{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":46.1,"y":57.1,"n":"Tabetha","s":1},{"z":"The Barrens","x":62.5,"y":35.4,"n":"Menara Voidrender","e":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"5216":{"id":5216,"t":"Target: Felstone Field","lv":53,"min":50,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Go to Felstone Field in Western Plaguelands to locate and defeat the Cauldron Lord present there. It may have a key that will allow access to the cauldron. You must have the Empty Felstone Field Bottle with you to secure a sample of the poisons used inside the cauldron.\nFelstone Field Cauldron Key Cauldron Lord Bilemaw\nEmpty Felstone Field Bottle\nProvided: Empty Felstone Field Bottle","desc":"Of the four cauldrons here in the west, the one located at Felstone Field may be the easiest one in obtaining access to. The Scourge have greener troops positioned here, though they should not be underestimated.\nGo to Felstone Field, northwest of Andorhal, and engage the cauldron lord there. We think it has a key that will unlock access to the cauldron. When unlocked, use this bottle to obtain a sample of the poisons inside the cauldron; we'll need it for study in developing a counter agent.","rew":"Experience: 5,250\n+100 reputation with Stormwind\n+100 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"An access panel to the cauldron remains securely fastened. In order to open it, you will need to find the key.","done":"The key taken from Cauldron Lord Bilemaw is a perfect fit in unlocking the access panel. A foul stench emanates from the opened panel as an unknown mix of concentrated substances swirl inside the cauldron.\nThere is a small spigot that the bottle fits well enough under, allowing you to draw a sample for High Priestess MacDonnell back at Chillwind Point.","pins":[{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":43,"y":84.5,"n":"High Priestess MacDonnell","s":1},{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":37.2,"y":56.8,"n":"Scourge Cauldron","e":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"5056":{"id":5056,"t":"Shy-Rotam","lv":60,"min":53,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Storm Shadowhoof at Everlook in Winterspring wants you to defeat Shy-Rotam.\nShy-Rotam slain","desc":"In northern Winterspring, great cats assemble around a large landmark called Frostsaber Rock. The leader of these cats is known by the name Shy-Rotam. Defeating the matriarch of the frostsabers would grant you much respect in the eyes of your fellow ‹race›.\nGo again to the harsh wilds, and once there, gather sacred meat from the frostsabers. Find the stone of Shy-Rotam, and place it there. Placing the meat of her kin before her will summon Shy-Rotam, in anger.\nBe ready for her fury, and defeat her.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nBeasthunter Dagger Beaststalker Blade\nExperience: 8,300\n+150 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"Shy-Rotam is bold and unforgiving; she will defend her kind with fervent enthusiasm.","done":"You have proven both your strength and your determination. Many more challenges await you, but I have already shown you as much as I am able.\nGood luck, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"Winterspring","x":61.9,"y":38.4,"n":"Storm Shadowhoof","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["winterspring"]},"94896":{"id":94896,"t":"Aid for the refugees","lv":11,"min":8,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Collect 8 Abandoned Belongings from the ruins of Ban'aethal.\n8 Abandoned Belongings","desc":"You look like a capable adventurer. Do you happen to be headed towards Shadowgale Forest? Ban'aethal lies deep in the forest; that's where we're all from.\n<Ealaane gestures to the other refugees.>\nWe've recently had to evacuate Ban'aethal, as it began to fall into the sky. It was sudden and in the middle of the night. If you are headed that way, would you please look for any belongings left behind? The forest and village are far too dangerous for us to return to now.","back":"So many of us left with nothing more than the clothes on our backs. Any belongings you might recover would be cherished.","done":"Thank you, ‹class›, you have done a great kindness to us refugees this day. I will make sure to return these to their owners. At least it gives us a place to start over from.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":65.8,"y":74.4,"n":"Ealaane Nimbuswalker","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]}});